From ef19691ab26e77353afecd03e93745149df8131f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhananjay Chauhan <dhananjay.chauhan@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2025 05:04:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 080/190] misc: xilinx-ai-engine: fix variable length array
 issue

commit 4a67cf2c771dcd8f8d93608de9b612a3a22edb46 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

While declaring an array, its size was given as a variable length,
which caused compilation warnings. Replace the variable length array
with a fixed length array to resolve these warnings.

Signed-off-by: Dhananjay Chauhan <dhananjay.chauhan@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20250901120412.1488041-1-dhananjay.chauhan@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-aie2ps.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-aie2ps.c b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-aie2ps.c
index 943fc37872b7..57b23cf327de 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-aie2ps.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-aie2ps.c
@@ -3378,7 +3378,7 @@ static ssize_t aie2ps_get_tile_sysfs_bd_metadata(struct aie_partition *apart,
 	ttype = aie2ps_get_tile_type(apart->adev, loc);
 	enabled = aie_part_check_clk_enable_loc(apart, loc);
 	for (u32 bd = 0; bd < dma_attr->num_bds; bd++) {
-		u32 bd_data[dma_attr->num_bd_regs];
+		u32 bd_data[AIE_MAX_BD_SIZE];
 		u32 i, index, base_bdoff;
 		u64 value;
 
-- 
